 "notes": "Continuation of Table XV Part I. The right half of the page (Tipura, Kachha Naga) is printed skewed: figures sit up to about half a row above their labels; rows were assigned by sequence counting within each column (e.g. Tipura 363/107/256 is the 5th district row = Lushai Hills; Tipura 1/1 is on the Nowgong line, with Lalung 4,822; Kachha Naga 7,282 = Manipur State; Tipura 321 = Khasi States). Lalung, Khasi States males: italic figure reads 101 at zoom (middle glyph an oval without tail), but British Territory 4,089 + 101 = 4,190 vs ASSAM 4,280, and 344 - 153 = 191, so 191 is intended; kept as read (101). Header of Dimasa printed \"Dimasa or Hills Kachari\"."
